  <p>
    Good instructions are specific (exact naming patterns, not "use good names"), give an example of the preferred pattern
    and put the most important rules first. Full samples, including a prompt file, are in the
    <a href={`${href('config-reference')}#github-copilot-instruction-files`}>Configuration reference</a>.
  </p>

  <h3 id="connect-to-mcp-server-endpoints">Connect to MCP server endpoints</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-slate">
      <thead><tr><th>Target</th><th>MCP option</th><th>How you connect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>SQL Server, Azure SQL, SQL database in Fabric</td>
          <td>MSSQL extension tools</td>
          <td>Built in: connect in the extension and use agent mode — no separate server to configure</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>SQL Server, Azure SQL, SQL database in Fabric</td>
          <td><strong>SQL MCP Server</strong> (Data API builder 2.x)</td>
          <td>Enable <code>runtime.mcp</code> in <code>dab-config.json</code>, run <code>dab start</code>, then add the <code>/mcp</code> URL (HTTP) or run DAB with <code>--mcp-stdio</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Fabric lakehouse, warehouse, semantic model</td>
          <td>Fabric <strong>data agent</strong> published as an MCP server</td>
          <td>Publish the data agent, copy the MCP server URL, add it as an HTTP server; sign in with Entra ID</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Azure resources broadly</td>
          <td>Azure MCP Server</td>
          <td>Install it, sign in to Azure, then use agent mode</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    In VS Code, add servers with <strong>MCP: Add Server</strong> or by editing <code>.vscode/mcp.json</code>, then check in
    agent mode's tools picker that the server is running and its tools are listed. Troubleshooting follows the usual
    order: JSON syntax (server missing), expired sign-in (authentication failed), firewall (timeout), permissions (empty
    schema).
  </p>
  <Callout type="tip" title="SQL MCP Server tools are generated from configuration">
    <p>
      SQL MCP Server exposes seven DML tools — <code>describe_entities</code>, <code>create_record</code>,
      <code>read_records</code>, <code>update_record</code>, <code>delete_record</code>, <code>execute_entity</code> and
      <code>aggregate_records</code> — and only for entities and roles your <code>dab-config.json</code> allows. Agents
      never see raw SQL access, so DAB permissions are the guardrail. Turning <code>delete-record</code> off globally is a
      common production setting.
    </p>
  </Callout>
